Subject: Netlink: Ignore address updates on down interfaces

Skip the work for an interface that is not administratively up. This
matters for a down interface that holds many addresses, such as
kube-ipvs0.

Squashed from these projectcalico/bird commits, oldest first. Each keeps
its author and message.

commit 3d15998f2410ff7043dbaa96879e2d9a11b1c3dc
Author: Dmitry Ilyevsky <dilyevsky@render.com>
Date:   2022-11-21

    [proto/device] Ignore addr updates on DOWN ifcs

    Ignores netlink addr updates for interfaces that *do not* have
    UP admin state. Improves performance for kube-ipvs* interfaces with
    large number of addresses.

commit 38f4c6e474b997d9780347482102e39b4bb60d27
Author: Bogdan Luca <luca.bogdan@gmail.com>
Date:   2023-12-29

    Remove spammy debug log message.
---
 sysdep/linux/netlink.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sysdep/linux/netlink.c b/sysdep/linux/netlink.c
index 27cec042..f4fb9f7e 100644
--- a/sysdep/linux/netlink.c
+++ b/sysdep/linux/netlink.c
@@ -744,6 +744,11 @@ nl_parse_addr(struct nlmsghdr *h, int scan)
       return;
     }
 
+  if (!(ifi->flags & IF_ADMIN_UP)) /* Ignore addresses for DOWN interfaces. */
+    {
+      return;
+    }
+
   bzero(&ifa, sizeof(ifa));
   ifa.iface = ifi;
   if (ifa_flags & IFA_F_SECONDARY)
